    "long_instructions": "# Interactivity in Web Apps\r\n\r\n#### When you visit a website or open an app, you’re not just looking at information—you’re doing something with it. \r\n#### Interactivity is what turns a static page into an engaging experience. It’s what allows users to click, tap, type, scroll, or hover to make something happen.\r\n\r\n#### **Interactive elements come in many forms:**\r\n\r\n- #### **Buttons** that trigger actions\r\n\r\n- #### **Menus** that expand or collapse\r\n\r\n- #### **Search bars** that respond as you type\r\n\r\n- #### **Icons** that change color or shape when hovered over\r\n\r\n#### These small moments of feedback and response are what make a web app feel alive and user-friendly.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #f3e5f5; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #9c27b0; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px\">\r\n      <strong>⚙️ Interactivity</strong>\r\n        is the ability of a software application or website to respond to user input\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/59c9b8a356ff4e56ec8c802ba5718b37-image-1684269154206.png\" alt=\"A clipboard with the words TO DO on it. This icon is used to signal an action item for participants.\" width=\"30px\" style=\"border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0px 10px 5px 0px;\"> \r\n\r\n#### Take a look at the website image below.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"\r\n  display: flex;\r\n  justify-content: center;\r\n  align-items: center;\r\n  max-width: 1000px;\r\n  margin: 20px auto;\r\n\">\r\n  <img \r\n    src=\"https://images.code.org/582df09f74b0f4858ad96c0b75d045f0-image-1760992309979.png\" \r\n    alt=\"amazon website 2025\"\r\n    style=\"width: 80%; max-width: 800px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.25);\"\r\n  >\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Discussion\r\n\r\n>- #### Where do you notice interactive elements?\r\n>- #### What kinds of interactions (tap, click, hover, type) are possible?\r\n>- #### How might those interactions help or guide the user?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
